;Standalone build of the MSX-DOS 2.20 style boot sector code that the
;kernel's built-in FORMAT command puts on FDD disks (bank2/bootsect.mac,
;included by bank6/dskfmt.mac as part of the kernel build).
;
;The tools-disk target assembles this file and links it with DATA.REL and
;DOS_CALLS.REL (which provide the KBUF, BDOS and DOS function number
;symbols) at address 0C01Eh, where boot sector code runs; the resulting
;binary is then written at offset 1Eh of the generated disk image's boot
;sector, right after the disk parameter block created by mformat, with the
;rest of the sector zeroed beforehand (the boot code relies on the bytes
;that follow it being zero, which is also what FORMAT does).
;
;This is what makes the disk image bootable in MSX-DOS 1 mode too.
;
;The MKDSK tool includes the resulting binary for the MSX-DOS 2 boot
;sectors that it creates, and another build of this file with the
;DOS1_BOOT_SECTOR symbol defined (no VOL_ID block) for the MSX-DOS 1 ones.

	name('tdboot')

	INCLUDE	macros.inc
	INCLUDE	const.inc

	INCLUDE	bank2/bootsect.mac

	end
